# Modular curves, part III: target signatures

The roadmap is README.md; this file is not the roadmap. It would state the roadmap's
headline theorems against the pinned APIs, but this roadmap owns no headline theorem:
every result of the Bakker–Tsimerman route is a target of the roadmap GeometricFreyMazur,
and it is stated, or recorded as not statable, in that roadmap's acceptance file.

* Geometric Frey–Mazur over a one-variable function field (BT16 Theorem 2) and full
  determinant-one torsion monodromy on a bounded-gonality base are statable at the pins
  and are stated there; they are not restated here.
* Geometric Frey–Mazur over the original open base (BT16 Theorem 1) lacks the relative
  elliptic-scheme and finite étale torsion-isomorphism carriers.
* Bounded-gonality rigidity on the diagonal quotient surface `Z(p)` (BT16 Theorems 3
  and 29) and its bounded-genus, rational/elliptic-curve and minimal-model corollaries
  (BT16 Corollaries 30–32) lack the quotient surface, its Hecke curves, cyclic quotient
  resolution and contraction carriers.
* Abramovich's linear gonality bound (ABR96 Theorem 0.1) lacks the compact algebraic
  congruence-curve carrier.
-/

